vrpr is derived from PyVRP
==========================

vrpr brings PyVRP (https://github.com/PyVRP/PyVRP, https://pyvrp.org) to R.
PyVRP is the work of Niels A. Wouda, Leon Lan, Wouter Kool and the PyVRP
contributors. Two parts of vrpr come from it:

  1. The C++ core under src/vendor/pyvrp/ is a copy of PyVRP's pyvrp/cpp
     directory. The upstream version is recorded in
     src/vendor/pyvrp/pyvrp_version.txt (PyVRP v0.14.0). The files are taken
     verbatim except for small portability fixes, listed in that file's notes;
     PyVRP's pybind11 bindings and spdlog-based logging are NOT included and
     are replaced by the cpp11 binding layer in src/.

  2. Parts of the R code are ports to R of PyVRP's Python code, not original
     designs: R/ils.R is a port of PyVRP's IteratedLocalSearch
     (pyvrp/IteratedLocalSearch.py) and R/penalty.R is a port of PyVRP's
     PenaltyManager (pyvrp/PenaltyManager.py). The model builder (R/model.R)
     and the stopping criteria (R/stop.R) are the R equivalents of PyVRP's
     Model and pyvrp.stop, and follow their interface.

The algorithms, the solver design and the performance are PyVRP's. Please
cite:

  Wouda, N. A., Lan, L., & Kool, W. (2024). PyVRP: a high-performance VRP
  solver package. INFORMS Journal on Computing, 36(4), 943-955.
  doi:10.1287/ijoc.2023.0055

vrpr is an independent project. It is not affiliated with, maintained by or
endorsed by the PyVRP project or its authors.

